    {"q": "If both parents carry an autosomal recessive condition, what is the chance that each child is affected?", "o": ["0 %", "25 %", "50 %", "100 %"], "a": 1, "x": "25 % in each pregnancy, 50 % of being a carrier and 25 % of not having the variant.", "tema": "herencia"},
    {"q": "A person with an autosomal dominant condition: what is the chance of passing it to each child?", "o": ["25 %", "50 %", "75 %", "100 %"], "a": 1, "x": "50 %, because one of their two copies of the gene is passed on at random.", "tema": "herencia"},
    {"q": "Why does haemophilia almost always affect males?", "o": ["Because it depends on male hormones", "Because the gene is on the X chromosome", "Because the gene is on the Y chromosome", "Because it is only passed from father to son"], "a": 1, "x": "Males have only one X, so one altered copy is enough. An affected father never passes it to his sons.", "tema": "herencia"},
    {"q": "Who do we inherit mitochondrial DNA from?", "o": ["Our father", "Our mother", "Both equally", "Neither: it forms anew"], "a": 1, "x": "The sperm's mitochondria do not pass into the embryo, so mitochondrial DNA comes from the mother.", "tema": "herencia"},
    {"q": "In blood group AB both alleles are expressed at once. What is this called?", "o": ["Complete dominance", "Codominance", "Recessiveness", "Imprinting"], "a": 1, "x": "In codominance both alleles show their effect at the same time.", "tema": "herencia"},
    {"q": "If the heritability of height is 0.8, what does that mean?", "o": ["That 80 % of your height comes from your genes", "That 80 % of the differences in height in that population are associated with genetic differences", "That height cannot be changed", "That 80 % of people are tall"], "a": 1, "x": "Heritability is about differences within a particular population, not about individuals.", "tema": "herencia"},
